mantle rm408
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rmx_florence_pennock
title the travelling seal
fits stage=adult|old
prefers piety=devout talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk wraps_a_whetstone_separately_from_sealed_letters
likes honey_cakes dancing festival_bells thunder
dislikes smoke haggling
fears having_to_answer_for_a_broken_seal
hopes placing_a_long_carried_letter_in_the_right_palm
topics travel +0.6 faith +0.5 pastimes +0.3 work +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# wraps the whetstone apart from any sealed letter and marks an unsuccessful call with a quiet turn of the heel.
words
oath! = Crumble my corner wax | Snarl my satchel seam
saying! = A shut door is half a journey | Keep the seal facing air
waxrim = a red rim of wax | a smooth wax mound
stonewrap = a stout whetstone wrap | a strip of rough linen
straploop = a padded loop | a leather keeper
heelturn = a neat turning step | one quiet swivel
honeybite = a golden cake end | a sweet honeyed crumb
dryflap = a doubled dry flap | a tucked leather lip
bellnote = a round answering note | a falling bell tone
stepbeat = a single landing beat | a quiet toe tap
knifecase = a firm working sheath | a thin wooden sleeve
rainridge = a ridge of folded cloth | a small upright seam
nameface = a neat direction line | a clear written address

grown

opinion houses mixed 1 : A great House might have the courtesy to arrange for one reliable palm at the door where it expects its letters.
opinion watch mixed 1 : A seal in honest keeping deserves to travel without providing every curious uniform with entertainment.
opinion church for 2 : My day's journeys are easier to face when I've left a few words with the Bright One before starting.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : Say what the carrying costs. A wolf who haggles at every doorstep soon empties the whole day of anything else.
opinion festivals for 1 : A bell that calls us to dance has earned a different answer from my feet.
opinion road for 1 : Even a fruitless journey leaves the next corner a little better known.
line greet : I have a moment between one door and the next.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome. We'll leave the satchel shut while we speak.
line greet.return : You found me on a bit of level going.
line farewell : May the right palm be waiting when your errand brings you to the door.
line farewell.return : Take a dry turn where the eaves allow it.
line answer.how : Tired in a way a small cake might improve.
line ask.how : Did somebody open when your day's work came knocking?
line react.news : I'll hold that as carefully as a folded sheet.
line react.news.known : I recognise the direction written on that news.
line react.news.new : That is a new delivery to my ears.
line react.news.doubt : I'd look carefully at the seal on a tale so conveniently addressed.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd be happy to carry glad words another good stretch today.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd see that reached a quiet ear before a crowded room.
line decline : No, that fold belongs to the one whose name is on it.
line accept_decline : Then I'll carry my offer back unopened.
line reassure : A closed door today can still receive you kindly tomorrow.
line sympathise : I can stand beside you through the moment before the knock.
line thank : You made a tired set of steps somewhat shorter.
line deflect_thanks : My feet were already pointed towards the work.
line ack : That direction is clear on the first reading.
line accept_preclose : Walk on while you have an easy road.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=official
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# a sealed thing and an interesting thing are often the same object.
b : Do you ever wonder what's inside? | What stops you enquiring?
a : Certainly. Looking after it well and wondering privately are duties that can coexist. | I remember somebody paid for a delivery, not an extra reader.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know a grand door chiefly by its remarkable success at staying shut. | There's one fine entrance where I can perform my returning step almost from habit.
b : Do you leave the letter there?
a : I need the right palm, not a doorstep with a handsome view of the weather. | Not even on my weariest trip. A polished threshold never signed for anything.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Some mornings my shortest prayer is to finish with every seal as sound as it started.
b : No request for lighter work? | What if a recipient stays away?
a : A little energy for the ordinary load will suffice. My remaining route can be what it is. | Then the seal still faces the sky another morning. A prayer needn't end just because my first attempt has.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my whetstone carefully parted from the letter flap.
b : Afraid of the weight? | Why carry a stone on a walking errand?
a : The rough face would abrade wax even if the whole thing weighed no more than a leaf. | It's a habit and it's useful for a working edge. Neither needs to rub a private crease raw.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can turn away from an unanswered door with a perfectly good little dance step.
b : Does it ease the disappointment? | What if the door opens behind you?
a : The feet remember being glad of a turning step. The rest of me sometimes follows. | I turn back in time. I've had much more practice at the first half than the second.

scene faith_2
when topic=faith self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Festival bronze gives my feet permission to take some pleasure.
b : Can you tell a festival peal from any other? | Do you put the satchel down?
a : I can usually tell by the faces round me before the second stroke. | If its care has been handed over properly. I won't give a letter an unexpected evening of dancing.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Honey cake and important paper need separate lodgings.
b : Has a crumb ever got loose? | How do you eat on the road?
a : A crumb can be shaken free. Honey will attach itself to the whole correspondence with alarming devotion. | Stop long enough to wrap the sweet bit and clean my fingers before moving the flap again.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder can answer a timid knock on an entirely different scale.
b : Would you wait for a gap? | Does the noise trouble you?
a : If there's time. The grandest rumble in the world can't inform a household that I've reached its side door. | I like it from somewhere under sound boards with a good flap between the letter and the rain.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I won't pretend carrying over a hill costs the same effort as crossing one street. | If somebody bargains over the walk I invite a look at the soles.
b : Suppose the figure startles somebody?
a : I can explain it without a raised voice. Anybody can decline the service. | The hill will be waiting when tomorrow comes. An honest price will travel just as well then.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let myself be tired until my boots reach the step, then stand straight before the knock.
b : Why conceal it? | Does standing straight help?
a : I don't need the household to feel indebted to my legs before we've found the right name. | It lets a full breath in and reminds the satchel where it's meant to hang.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A friend gets precisely the same unopened letter a stranger would receive.
b : Wouldn't a friend tell you the contents? | Isn't there some favour you can do?
a : That's a choice for after delivery. Till then I know as little as the stranger. | I can choose a quiet time to knock where my duty gives me the choice.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hang my satchel with a finger's width between the wax and the wall.
b : Does it need so much care at home? | What happens if the wall's warm?
a : A letter can be handed in splendidly dry and be damaged in the final inch. I'd rather mind the inch. | I move the hook away from the warmth. A seal can lose its face without anybody breaking it.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count an unanswered visit as some work done, even when the paper hasn't left my hands.
b : What have you delivered? | Would the sender agree?
a : Myself to the right place. The letter has been a blameless and inactive travelling companion. | I'd tell the truth about what I found and let that stand for itself.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A particular letter once became so familiar I recognised its corner through my coat.
b : Did that make you want to open it? | Did you ever get used to the wait?
a : No. Familiarity ought to make me a better keeper, not a second addressee. | Enough to remember a cake on the return journey. It didn't reduce the distance but improved the company.

scene weather_2
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke is worse than ordinary dirt on a satchel flap.
b : Does it get into the letter? | Can you brush the stain away?
a : The smell can. I would hate to have a harmless delivery announce a fire to a worried nose. | Some. I'd sooner carry the bag round the nearest clear corner than spend all evening rubbing the flap.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In tight weeks I pack enough bread for an unsuccessful trip as well as the one I set out to finish.
b : Why two pieces? | What if the door opens at once?
a : It saves me buying a costly late supper because hope packed lighter than sense. | Then a spare bite can wait in its cloth or go to a hungrier palm.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a newcomer the way to a door and some idea of how best to announce a visit.
b : Isn't knocking simple? | Would you go along?
a : Which entrance and how loudly can be a puzzle at a grand house. A good direction can save a scolding. | As far as my own errand allows. Most of the trouble goes once a latch is in sight.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The open talk says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. It wasn't read off anything I've carried.
b : Do you put much faith in it? | Would you repeat a name from your satchel?
a : Open talk can travel faster than written sense. I'll reserve judgment till it has travelled intact. | Not to decorate a public story. A name I carry under a flap stays under my care.

story wax [topic=work]
  : I once put a cake of hard wax beside a stone wrap and reached for the wrong one in poor light.
  : The stone looked unusually festive by the time I'd rubbed the two together.
  b : Did it damage a letter?
  : Just my dignity. I was practising at my own table, which is the proper place for an expensive piece of foolishness.

story return [topic=memories]
  : I took my neat half turn at a shut door and found a little pup imitating it behind me.
  : We did the half turn twice and ended up facing the closed door again.
  b : Did anyone answer that time?
  : Still no answer. At least the walk acquired a willing partner for one short figure.

story sweet [topic=food]
  : A bit of honey cake worked loose in an outer pocket and stuck to a dry whetstone wrapper.
  : I sat on a low step and picked crumbs off the paper one at a time.
  b : Was it worth rescuing?
  : I found the pause was worth more than the crumbs. I ate the piece that had stayed in its own cloth.

rule @seal
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wax facing out and rough stone turned away. | Some words travel better without a curious thumb on them.

rule @storm
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Knock between the great noises and listen in the little space. | That thunder could announce a whole street of callers.

rule @turn
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A quiet heel turn and the letter keeps its journey. | An unanswered door needn't hear a temper leaving.

rule @tired
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Long evening roads improve a small cake wonderfully. | There's a little more walking left in my soles.
dlg resident.hub : Your voice carries nicely to the shoulder with the strap on it.
dlg resident.job [self.job=official] : At #self.workplace# I keep track of what reached the right hands and what still calls for another journey.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : What has come into open hearing is this. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : A street account says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's public talk, quite apart from anything sealed.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, this meeting has spared me at least one knock.
dlg resident.bye : I hope the door you're bound for is ready for your hand.

graft resident.hub
choice Do you ever tire of carrying an undelivered letter? -> wax_route
node wax_route
say The legs do, certainly. But if I've failed three times to find the right person, the fourth attempt isn't an excuse for handing it to the wrong one.
choice How long can you keep it safe? -> wax_wait
choice Keep the seal safe. -> hub
node wax_wait
say On the next trip I'll look after the wax and bring back an exact account of how things stand. After that there will be another small decision to make.
choice Keep the seal safe. -> hub
